menu "PRISM on the Korvo-1"

    config PRISM_LCD_PCLK_MHZ
        int "RGB panel pixel clock (MHz)"
        default 18
        range 1 40
        help
            The panel's pixel clock. 18 MHz is the board-support package's own value
            (BSP_DISPLAY_PANEL_RGB_TIMING). Lower it if the picture shifts: the panel then reads
            less from PSRAM per second, at a lower refresh rate.

    config PRISM_DISPLAY_CPU_COPY
        bool "Copy the bands into the panel buffer on the CPU instead of the PPA"
        default n
        help
            The fallback if the PPA misbehaves: each band PRISM draws is copied into the panel's
            buffer by the CPU, which then cannot draw the next band meanwhile.

endmenu
